#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087843 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087545 :question/id #uuid "011cf746-baa5-5395-8515-3beb98ff22a4" :question/math-academy-id "e-5302" :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x) = \\dfrac{x-2}{x^2-6x+8}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-6x+8} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-2}{(x-2)(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x-2}}{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nx - 4 = 0\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $x = 4.$ Therefore, $x = 4$ is the only vertical asymptote."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "53b26ee4-53af-5660-a9e6-8e5cca8b3e1d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049181 :topic/math-academy-id 423 :topic/title "Simplifying Rational Expressions by Factoring"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890b8337-3605-5539-bf84-de88d0671ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x =-2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085645} {:answer/id #uuid "bb07a5bd-4864-579b-b0a4-d2fa7187f553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085646} {:answer/id #uuid "3043a706-6fe7-524d-83d2-2b26cf05e66a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-2, x = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085647} {:answer/id #uuid "5aaf2864-92f8-5242-add4-be5b354019b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085648} {:answer/id #uuid "758788a8-b3b6-5d98-a458-d212cc992dd5" :answer/ty